{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And his brothers envied him.</b> Know that hatred, for the most part, comes from jealousy. The hatred mentioned above — ״וישנאו אותו״ — was on account of the jealousy of love, as it is written: ״ויראו אחיו כי אותו אהב אביהם מכל אחיו וישנאו אותו״. If so, why did it repeat here, ״ויקנאו בו אחיו״? It may be explained that at first they were not jealous of him on account of any superiority he had over them, but only on account of the jealousy of the father's love, since he loved him more than them — and why should they be jealous of him when they were older than he, and he was a lad of seventeen years, and a person is not jealous of his fellow except of one like him and his equal? But now, after he told his dreams and they were wiser than the wise in interpretation, they saw that he was destined to reign, and jealousy clothed them in this. This is the force of ״ויקנאו בו״ — it does not say ״ויקנאו אותו״ as in (Genesis 26:14) ״ויקנאו אותו פלשתים״, but בו — in him, concerning the superiority they saw in him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:16.061990825Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}